# ==================================================================================
# Added by t/live-stack — rules for the Plan Reader / Bid Assistant / frontend stack
# ==================================================================================

# --- Secrets (NEVER commit) ---
.env
**/.env
*.env
!**/.env.example

# --- SQLite / databases (client bid data + regenerable) ---
# Pattern-based on purpose: an exact-path rule matched 1 of 9 db files in the
# source repo and left ~1.1 GB of client data stageable.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.bak
*.bak_*

# --- Vector store (Chroma persist dir; rebuilds on ingest, ~1.5 GB) ---
# Path-relative on purpose: exact-path rules were coupled to the pre-restructure
# `02_modules/plan_reader/` layout and stopped matching the moment the module moved,
# which would have committed ~6 GB of derived artifacts into a shared repo's history.
**/06_chroma/
**/chroma_db/

# --- Plan Reader: client plan PDFs + regenerable per-plan artifacts (~4.5 GB) ---
**/00_input/plans/**/*.pdf
**/00_input/plans/**/*.md
**/00_input/plans/**/*.json
**/00_input/_md_cache/
**/00_input/_report_payload_cache/
**/00_input/_report_competitor_prediction_cache/
**/00_input/_report_raw_extraction_cache/
# 02_outputs/ is generated diagnostics + scorecards — regenerable, ignored wholesale.
# The 7 files old `main` tracked here remain recoverable at d63b96c if ever needed as
# cited evidence of extraction quality.
**/plan_reader/02_outputs/

# --- CI model: large regenerable training/eval outputs ---
# Deliberately file-pattern, NOT `03_training/outputs/`. That directory is 96 MB but only because
# of ranking_predictions.csv (94 MB); it also holds the *_model.json files — including
# logistic_baseline_model.json, the orchestrator's --model input — at ~30 KB total. A directory-level
# ignore would drop those and silently break live report generation on a fresh clone, while still
# passing locally because the working tree already has them.
#
# ranking_predictions.csv must be regenerated or obtained on a fresh clone: see
# pipelines/ci_model/README.md. Everything ignored here is a *write* target of 03_training /
# 04_evaluation; the 06_reporting path reads none of it (verified).
**/ranking_predictions.csv
**/top_k_precision.csv
**/top_k_recall.csv
**/*_tuning.csv
# Kept tracked on purpose: **/*_model.json, shallow_decision_tree.{json,txt} — small, and a fresh
# clone cannot generate a report without them.

# --- Bid Assistant: captured chat traffic (contains client bid data) ---
**/data/conversations/
**/data/corrections/
**/.chainlit/
**/.files/
**/.deepeval/

# --- Frontend (Next.js) ---
node_modules/
.next/
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# --- Python / OS cruft ---
.venv/
venv/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- research/sweet_spot ---
# Exported notebook renders (4 files, 4.5 MB). Regenerable from the .ipynb/.Rmd
# sources, which ARE tracked, and nothing references them.
# Scoped to this directory deliberately: a bare `*.html` rule is occurrence 1 in
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 7 -- a pattern that stopped matching what it was
# written for. Everything else under research/sweet_spot/, including all of
# outputs/, is TRACKED on purpose. Do not add a blanket outputs/ ignore here.
research/sweet_spot/notebooks/*.html
research/sweet_spot/notebooks/*_files/

# Spec books (2026-08-10): ~25 MB of state DOT PDFs, reference only, never needed to RUN.
# Kept on disk, excluded from the repo. The derived lookup (2026-08-10-spec_item_lookup.csv) IS tracked.
pipelines/plan_reader/05_knowledge/*.pdf

# Timestamped backups of cleared payload-cache entries (2026-08-10 re-warm). Recoverable
# local artifacts, same class as the cache itself, which is already ignored above.
**/00_input/_report_payload_cache_backup_*/

# Handoff cleanup 2026-08-17 — archived-out material, retained locally only
20260817_handoff_archive/
.claude/
